WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.300
Detection ideas can come from threat intelligence, incident lessons, threat hunting, red team exercises, vulnerability disclosures, business risks, compliance requirements, and analyst feedback.

2
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.204
Not every idea deserves immediate development.

3
00:00:16.204 --> 00:00:24.565
Teams should prioritize based on relevance, expected value, available telemetry, impact, likelihood, and operational capacity.

4
00:00:24.565 --> 00:00:29.654
Prioritization prevents the detection backlog from becoming a random pile of requests.

5
00:00:29.654 --> 00:00:35.890
It helps teams focus on detections that are feasible, useful, and connected to meaningful defensive outcomes.

6
00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:38.903
A good intake process also captures context.

7
00:00:38.903 --> 00:00:46.466
The team should know who requested the detection, what behavior matters, what data may be needed, and how success will be recognized.
